    "description": "Natural Mineral Specimen Lot\nCrystals, Geodes, and Raw Stones\n9 Pieces, 10.8 lbs\nA diverse collection of nine natural mineral specimens featuring a variety of textures, colors, and crystal formations. This lot is anchored by a significant blue celestite geode, accompanied by various quartz and amethyst specimens. These earth-mined pieces are ideal for geological study, crystal collections, or as natural decorative accents, showcasing the unique crystalline structures formed over geological time.\n9 unique natural earth-mined specimens including celestite, quartz, and amethyst\nLarge celestite (celestine) geode with pale blue crystal clusters in a grey matrix\nAssorted quartz specimens including a clear point, a white cluster, and three druzy geode halves\nAmethyst specimens including a chevron amethyst chunk and a small point\nBanded polychrome jasper or mineral specimen in red and brown tones\nTotal lot weight of 10.8 pounds\nCondition:\nAll specimens are in natural, raw, or semi-polished condition. The celestite geode features a solid outer matrix with well-defined interior crystals. Quartz and amethyst pieces show natural terminations and facets, with typical natural inclusions and minor surface variations inherent to earth-mined minerals. No visible repairs or artificial coloring. Surfaces are clean with minor natural dust in deep crystal recesses.",
